  "method": "V279 source picks wide/narrow W2 from live routes. Each physical CTA processes its strided jobs; work in issued tensor rows x N channels, full K shared. Full-wave occupancy assumed at 128 or 132 CTAs under each shape. Perfect W13/W2 mixes ignore all data dependencies, register/cluster constraints, nonlinear costs and synchronization. Window estimates reset the persistent grid at expert boundaries and preserve the initial full-shape geometry; a smaller real call may select a different kernel. These are issue-unit bounds, not device timings."
